afk: eval cells default to a 300 s deadline, the same as bash.

Why: afk disables the bash tool, so eval is the command runner. Upstream
gives bash a 300 s default but eval only 30 s; removing bash silently cut
the default command deadline from 5 minutes to 30 seconds. ssh/network
commands routinely exceed 30 s, and a timed-out cell whose kernel does not
answer the interrupt gets the whole kernel killed (observed 2026-10-04 nmm
session: rec 4980, then cascading kernel deaths).

What must survive a rebase:
- TOOL_TIMEOUTS.eval.default is 300 (min/max unchanged). Explicit
  `timeout` values and `timeout: 0` behave as upstream.
- test/tools/eval-auto-background.test.ts asserts the default deadline in
  the auto-background notice; it expects 300s. Since 18.18.0 upstream's
  test/tools/eval-timeout-contract.test.ts also asserts the omitted-deadline
  default; its row expects 300.

